WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.160
NCIS' Michael Weatherly didn't initially&nbsp;
say why he left the show, but his real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.067
reason for leaving was surprisingly romantic&nbsp;
— but not for the reasons you might expect!

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:13.080
Stars who have been a part of the show have all&nbsp;
had their disparate reasons for leaving – and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.980
those reasons haven't always been transparent&nbsp;
from the start. Pauley Perrette, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.660
reportedly left after a workplace situation that&nbsp;
caused her discomfort led to conflict between her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.640
and Mark Harmon, which wasn't revealed at the time&nbsp;
of her departure. Sasha Alexander, who played Kate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.080
Todd, apparently felt the shooting schedule was&nbsp;
too difficult, which makes sense since the show is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.520
infamous for long shooting days. Her replacement,&nbsp;
Cote de Pablo, felt her character wasn't getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.801
enough respect and the scripts weren't worthy&nbsp;
of her, as she revealed in a 2016 interview.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:43.740
When Michael Weatherly left at the&nbsp;
end of the show's 13th season in 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.040
it was an emotional ending given&nbsp;
that his character, Tony DiNozzo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.802
was one of the original NCIS agents&nbsp;
and a major lead in the series.

00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:54.640
"I'm going home to see Tali."

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.320
When Michael Weatherly's exit was announced,&nbsp;
no reason was given for his departure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.880
although The Hollywood Reporter linked the news to&nbsp;
an incident in which Weatherly pleaded no contest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.380
to driving under the influence and was sentenced&nbsp;
to an alcohol recovery program. Over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.640
however, he's given a few reasons for leaving.&nbsp;
When announcing his new legal drama Bull,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.000
he explained during the Television&nbsp;
Critics Association's press tour,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.480
"I was burnt out by 'NCIS' and I&nbsp;
was ready for a new challenge."

00:01:18.591 --> 00:01:21.051
He explained that he was&nbsp;
tired of the grind, saying,

00:01:21.051 --> 00:01:24.120
"It really felt like a circle that&nbsp;
had gone all the way around and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.300
really felt happy with the resolution&nbsp;
of character and my time on the show."

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.200
He also told TV Insider that he was&nbsp;
experiencing wanderlust and that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.620
were other things he wanted to do. Plus,&nbsp;
he wished to spend time with his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.060
which includes his physician wife Bojana&nbsp;
Jankovic, their children, and a son from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.400
his previous marriage. NCIS is well known for&nbsp;
its long hours. Actor Sean Murray told StarryMag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.440
in 2020 that the average workday was 12 hours for&nbsp;
the actors, which was an improvement over previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.813
years. As noted, those hours drove colleague&nbsp;
Sasha Alexander away after just two seasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:59.400
So this wasn't surprising — Weatherly had,&nbsp;
after all, been on the show for 13 seasons.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.240
But Michael Weatherly has also said he had&nbsp;
another reason for leaving, one that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.620
more romantic. It has everything to do with&nbsp;
the romance between his character and Ziva.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.760
"I did not want you to find me, and yet you did."

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.520
Their sexual tension ignited in the third season&nbsp;
and continued its slow and sometimes frustrating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.480
burn throughout the seasons until Cote de Pablo&nbsp;
announced her departure and her character was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.980
killed off — except, she wasn't really dead.&nbsp;
Watchers of the show know that DiNozzo later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.629
discovered that he and Ziva had a child and when&nbsp;
Tony left, it was to take care of their daughter.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.700
"Well, thank God for the go-bag, right?"

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.380
In the TV Insider interview, Weatherly noted&nbsp;
that he started thinking about leaving after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.315
de Pablo left in NCIS' 11th season.&nbsp;
The reason? He told the publication,

00:02:45.315 --> 00:02:48.864
"Their great dynamic, the badinage and&nbsp;
sparring and flirting between those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.864 --> 00:02:52.620
two characters and how they would swing from&nbsp;
siblings to near lovers and back to buddies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.700
that was gone, and then I got to the point&nbsp;
where I felt I'd stayed at the party for too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.600
long. I would look around the room and other&nbsp;
people were really in sync and having fun."

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.880
De Pablo has since made several guest appearances&nbsp;
on NCIS, revealing that Ziva had actually faked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.740
her death. She and DiNozzo were apparently&nbsp;
reunited in 2019, although technically Weatherly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.600
hasn't been seen on the series since he departed.&nbsp;
However, the actor posted a recent New Year's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.760
tweet hinting that an on-screen reunion might be&nbsp;
coming in 2023. Fans will want to stay tuned.

